Message-ID: <9509210705.AA08917@foo.garply.com>
Date: Thu, 21 Sep 1995 02:05:12 -0500
From: Aaron Sakovich <aaron@garply.com>
Subject: New on the archive

I've just uploaded avsview.zip, a demo version of the AVS data visualization
tool.  This is a 3D data presentation package with several demo files (e.g.,
a couple human faces, the Carribean, and the infamous Teapot, among others)
that you can pick up and move around in real time with your mouse.

It's a little sluggish on a low-end 166 MHz machine with a ZLXp-E1 graphics
adapter. This app takes advantage of OpenGL calls, so if you've got 3D
board, it should work very nicely.

This is a large download at just over 3.0MB.

A word of caution: I've crashed my machine twice now while running the
program full screen.  This is the first time I've crashed an Alpha running
anything other than early beta software that had conflicts with other
applications, and I've been running Alpha NT for almost 3 years now.
Running it at its default window size hasn't crashed the system yet, and
I've gone through all the models.

Enjoy,
Aaron

