>Gee, I just asked a similar question this morning. I'm dying for a decent
>VT-100 compatible telnet program for my AlphaNT workstation. 

The closest I've seen yet is PTerm -- it's an NT app, but IT DOESN'T RUN ON
ALPHA!  It runs on Intel, MIPS, and PoorerPC.  Why?  Cause the manufacturers
of those systems gave Felsina their machines to port it.  Digital didn't
help port the app (in spite of several requests, supposedly).

It sounds like one of those "critical" apps that fell through the cracks.

 Felsina Software, Inc.
 4440 Finley Ave., #108                    Internet: felsina@crl.com
 Los Angeles, CA 90027                     CIS: 74777,1006
 URL: http://www.crl.com/~felsina/         CIS Forum: GO ATALK

Anyone in Digital want to take the bull by the horns and get these folks in
touch with their porting center?  Get them a Jensen or a noname board?

I've not actually tried the emulator, but have read other folks' discussions
on it, and most seem pleased.

I've also used Anzio Lite (available from the Consumate WinSock Apps list --
see the application section of our JumpStation for a pointer) and it's not
half bad.  My biggest complaint is that it has no scroll bar...  8^(

Here's a list of the one's I've tested:

        UWterm          386
        EWAN            works
        trmptel         no <del> key
        wnqvt           386
        AnzioLite       no scroll bar
        yawtel          no <del> key

I use EWAN and AnzioLite, depending on if I need a scroll bar or not.

There's a list of 16 bit TE's on 

ftp://ftp.iquest.com/pub/windows/papa/telnet/00_index.txt

a mirror of papa.indstate.edu.  I've not tested them all -- if someone else
has any more data, publish it here please so we can get a complete list!

Aaron

