Hmmm, I'm not familiar with Gauss -- anyone else?  You could also check the
Alpha Apps catalog at:

        http://www-usa.partner.digital.com/app_search/bin/search

Oh, what the heck -- I just queried for Gauss and it came back with 0 entries.
You might want to contact the manufacturer to see if you can either persuade
them to port or get in on any beta program they've got.

Besides that, you're definitely not a year early.  MS Office has been out
for quite some time now.  As far as eXceed goes, I'm not sure if they've
ported to Alpha yet, but there's always the latest version of eXcursion from
Digital that is X11 R6 compliant.

The Internet is no big deal (evidence my existence here) but I've not tried
integrating with Banyan yet (not much call for it here).  Anyone else got
experiences in these areas?

>     I'm willing to put up with running in emulation mode as long as the 
>     performance is not too poor.  What kind of compatibility problems and 
>     performance does emulation yield?

Performance on the 233 and 266 XL should be rather good -- probably like a
486 at 66-100 MHz.  I don't notice performance anymore -- nearly all my
critical apps are native now, except Eudora -- and so what if it takes an
extra half-second to close or open a mail message...

There are definitely compatibility issues to contend with -- the standard NT
issues with VXD's and the issue of real-mode code for RISC processors.  But
the first is becoming less of an issue as more 32 bit drivers (although the
list is still kinda short -- see the HCL) are being written, and the latter
should disappear in the spring with the next release of NT -- Insignia
supposedly has the 486 code in beta now.

It's nothing unusual to run on an Alpha -- a lot of apps still run, and more
and more manufacturers are writing for the Alpha.  The biggest difference I
notice is when I have to work on an Intel processor...  Stuff that takes me
10 minutes on the Alpha, I have to sit and stew for an hour on a 486.  What
a waste.

YMMV, but I doubt by much.
Aaron

