It really depends upon the availability of tools.  Microsoft has a vested
interest in Windows NT but supports just a few languages across platforms.
If an application vendor want some language which is not a Microsoft
favorite,
such as Pascal, Fortran, Ada, Cobol, etc., they are dependent on a lot of
smaller
tool vendors who may not target non-Intel platforms at present.

andy@livingston.com (Andy Doolittle) writes:

