> prior life I managed a group of engineers porting applications to
> Alpha/OSF.  Some of the code out there is frightening - dividing the
> size of an array of pointers by a hardcoded 4 to determine the number of
> elements.  It is somewhat ironic that the cleanest code we came across,
> from an int vs long vs pointer point of view, was code that ran on DOS or
> Windows.  

Windows NT is only 32 bits, even on Alpha.  Where the hardware requires
64 bits, sign-extended values are used, but that is taken care of by the
compilers.

